  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 126 PM MDT Mon Sep 7 2026\n\nSatellite and radar imagery show main circulation associated\nwith PacNW trough has shifted northeast of the region, leaving\ndry slot and post-frontal air mass in place over East Idaho.\nBreezy winds continue through the Snake Plain with gusts 30-35\nmph across the northern portions of the region. Winds should\npeak by early afternoon, then decrease through the remainder of\nthe evening. Cool temperatures today behind the front give way\nto gradual warming beginning Tuesday and continuing through\nThursday along with dry conditions. Ensembles favor spoke of\nbroad trough dropping through the PacNW into the region by\nFriday, reintroducing a chance of precipitation by the weekend.\nWinds increase Thursday through Saturday in response, and winds\ncould approach Wind Advisory criteria with gusts exceeding 40 \nmph for both Thursday and Friday. There is slight differences in\ntiming of precipitation arrival between the NBM and the \nensemble means and clusters, but we could see a few showers and \nthunderstorms by late Friday, increasing into Saturday. The \nincrease in moisture should provide a slight cooling trend into \nthe weekend, as well.",
